     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended amlodipine dose for adults is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and prolonged vasodilation that is hard to reverse. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make that dose safe.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. That applies to any order, whatever its dose.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- If 50 mg was a typo, I can enter the standard dose of 5 mg by mouth once daily. Starting doses are usually 2.5\u20135 mg. A prescriber should confirm the dose and the indication first.\n- If the treating clinician really wants a dose above the maximum, they should enter or confirm it themselves. The order would also need pharmacy review.\n\nIf you give me the corrected dose, or the prescriber's confirmation, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
